<title>BELGIUM: AXA BELGIUM H1 1996 PROFIT 565 MLN BFR.</title>
<headline>AXA BELGIUM H1 1996 PROFIT 565 MLN BFR.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>    Net profit			565 vs    218</p>
<p>    Turnover		     10,126 vs 10,125</p>
<p>    Premium written	    10,336 vs  6,778</p>
<p>    Operating costs	     3,248 vs  2,374</p>
<p>    Technical charges	   7,710 vs  5,178</p>
<p>    Financial income	    1,848 vs  1,635</p>
<p>NOTE - AXA Belgium, the main unit in Belgium of France's AXA, said first-half 1996 earnings were not comparable with those of the year-earlier period following the merger on July 1, 1995, with Victoire Belgium NV. Victoire had a first-half 1995 net profit of 313 million francs.</p>
<p>Chief executive Patrick de Courcel told a news conference he expected further improvement of earnings in the second half.</p>
<p>AXA Belgium, of which 5.2 percent is quoted on the Brussels bourse, is part of the AXA Group in Belgium, which also comprises De Kortrijkse Verzekering, Juris and La Mutuelle Patronale. -- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6815</p>
</text>
